lized` and `notarized`; local mining only populates"," //! `finalized`. The certificate bytes are unprefixed hex."," //!","-//! Identity rotation takes effect in the epoch after the next block's epoch, allowing its","-//! predecessor's boundary block to announce the new key before it signs. Snapshots restore pending","-//! rotations exactly; rollback restores the retained block's key schedule.","+//! Identity rotation takes effect two epochs after the next block's epoch. The first boundary","+//! announces a full DKG for the intervening epoch; its final boundary publishes the new key before","+//! it signs. Snapshots restore pending rotations exactly; rollback restores the retained block's","+//! key schedule."," //!"," //! Locally mined fork blocks commit to a partial trie of the accounts and storage slots cached"," //! when the block was mined, rather than the complete upstream state. Non-pending `eth_getProof`"],"additions":4,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/anvil/tests/fixtures/tempo-consensus-compat/README.md","lines":["@@ -11,11 +11,13 @@ bytes, Ethereum block hashes and consensus digests must identify the same block."," Fork checks inherit skipped views from a native root in a nonzero epoch and verify"," that the next epoch restarts at view one with parent view zero."," ","-Rotation checks begin with one trusted identity, authenticate the boundary block,","-and decode its DKG outcome to obtain the next epoch's key. The next certificate","-must verify under that announced key and reject the old key. Snapshot replay","-must restore the same announcement and activation without trusting a fresh","-identity RPC response for each block.","+Rotation checks begin with one trusted identity and authenticate the boundary","+that announces a full DKG for the following epoch. Its output retains the old","+key, while its next players commit to the new committee. The following boundary","+publishes that committee's key under the old key's signature, and the 